  "details": "I have an idea y'all. Hear me out. \nSo, I watched the dev stream last night, and I thought of a way to do currency. For however many hours you spend in the game, you get points per hour. And if you go to public or friends+, you get more points per hour. Adding someone as a friend gets an extra boost of points (even by just one). Then to track and use these points, have a separate ui/world even to use the points to purchase accessories, such as vr pets. The more time you spend in vr with your pet, the pet grows up/evolves. These pets could be created by community model makers as a commission to give back to those creators. Pets could be ordinary pets, dragons, or even Pokemon-like creatures who can evolve forms. You could purchase points, but it is a lot easier (and still free) to just spend time in game to earn points. You could make the pets require food or energy to make people get in game more. This would encourage constant gameplay. You could buy accessories for the pets, or even just emblems for near your nameplate with the points if you don't want the responsibility of a pet. This could be a fun way to implement in-game currency while also encouraging constant gameplay in the community and giving back to model creators alike. \nVRChat user: heyitsjaayy",
